        "title": "Microtasks Always Run Before the Next Macrotask",
        "content": "The JS runtime executes synchronous code on the Call Stack. When clear, the engine drains the **entire Microtask Queue** (Promise callbacks, queueMicrotask) before picking a single Macrotask (setTimeout, setInterval).",
        "codeSnippet": "console.log('1');\nsetTimeout(() => console.log('2'), 0);\nPromise.resolve().then(() => console.log('3'));\nconsole.log('4');\n// Output: 1, 4, 3, 2",
