        "type": "pitfall",
        "badge": "03 // DANGER ZONE",
        "title": "Iterator Invalidation Prevention",
        "content": "Modifying a collection while iterating over it is a classic C++ crash. Rust's borrow checker rejects it at compile time!",
        "codeSnippet": "let mut v = vec![1, 2];\nfor i in &v { v.push(*i); } // Compiler rejects iterator invalidation!",
        "tip": "Hacker Rule: Collect modifications into a separate vector or index explicitly.",
